      "content": "5.1 Classical Arts"
    },
    {
      "id": "ntng566",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.1.1 Classical Dance"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Kuchipudi is the classical dance form of Telangana and Andhra Pradesh. Originating from Kuchipudi village in Krishna district (AP), it is characterized by fast rhythmic footwork, graceful body movements, and elaborate costumes. Bharatanatyam is also popular in Telangana.",
      "id": "6q0aw7z"
    },
    {
      "id": "njh9t7w",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.1.2 Perini Shivatandavam"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Perini Shivatandavam is an ancient classical dance form of Telangana that was revived after centuries of obscurity. It is a vigorous masculine dance performed in honor of Lord Shiva. It originated during the Kakatiya period and was performed before soldiers going to war. The dance was revived by Dr. Nataraja Ramakrishna in the 20th century.",
      "id": "d656u3z"
    },
    {
