    {
      "id": "yr4p5ew",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.4 Cuisine"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Telangana cuisine is characterized by its spicy flavors, extensive use of tamarind, and unique preparations that differ from Andhra cuisine:",
      "id": "80tmnpa"
    },
    {
      "id": "pgz32au",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Hyderabadi Biryani – World-famous; Dum biryani style; Kacchi Gosht ki Biryani",
        "Haleem – Slow-cooked meat and wheat dish; famous worldwide from Hyderabad; GI-tagged product",
        "Sarva Pindi (Sarapapindi) – Rice flour pancake",
        "Uppindi – Broken rice dish",
        "Jonna Rotte – Sorghum (Jowar) flatbread",
        "Sajja Rotte – Pearl millet flatbread",
        "Gongura Mutton – Made with sorrel leaves",
        "Irani Chai – Tea with buffalo milk and malai; specialty of Hyderabad",
        "Osmania Biscuits – Tea-time biscuit specialty of Hyderabad"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ihd2sit",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 2,
      "content": "5.5 Literature"
    },
    {
      "id": "fottp21",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.5.1 Telugu Literature"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Telugu is one of the classical languages of India. Telangana has a rich Telugu literary tradition:",
      "id": "7xuv7mo"
    },
    {
      "id": "n4cp2ap",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Nannaya Bhattaraka – First Telugu poet (11th century); wrote Mahabharata in Telugu",
        "Tikkana Somayaji – Second of the Kavitraya (trio); wrote parts of Mahabharata",
        "Errapragada – Third of Kavitraya; completed Mahabharata in Telugu",
        "Palkuriki Somanatha – Saint-poet; wrote in Dwipada style; devoted to Veerashaiva",
        "Potana – Wrote Maha Bhagavatamu; dedicated to Rama; refused Reddi kings' patronage"
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "l3rozfi",
      "type": "heading",
      "level": 3,
      "content": "5.5.2 Urdu Literature"
    },
    {
      "type": "paragraph",
      "content": "Hyderabad is a major center of Urdu literature in India. The Nizami period produced outstanding Urdu poets and writers:",
      "id": "p6raj9m"
    },
    {
      "id": "6vt51pa",
      "type": "list",
      "items": [
        "Dagh Dehlvi – Last great Mughal poet; lived in Hyderabad",
        "Mir Taqi Mir – Visited Hyderabad; influence on local poetry",
        "Muhammad Quli Qutb Shah – Qutb Shahi sultan; one of the earliest Urdu poets"
      ]
    },
    {
